{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"InnoRouterTesting"}],"title":"Throttling Rapid Navigation Taps","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Rate-limit navigation commands without threading timestamps through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every call site. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ThrottleNavigationMiddleware"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels commands that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrive within a minimum interval of a previously accepted command"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sharing the same key."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/innorouterswiftui\/tutorial-throttling"]}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/Tutorial-Throttling"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Scenario","level":2,"text":"Scenario"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Users double-tap a “Buy” button. The first tap pushes the purchase","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"screen; the second should be silently dropped. Rolling that logic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into every button is noise — middleware is the right layer.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Installation","level":2,"text":"Installation"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment","code":["let store = NavigationStore<AppRoute>(","    configuration: NavigationStoreConfiguration(","        middlewares: [","            .init(","                middleware: AnyNavigationMiddleware(","                    ThrottleNavigationMiddleware<AppRoute>(","                        interval: .milliseconds(300)","                    )","                ),","                debugName: \"throttle\"","            )","        ]","    )",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default initializer uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"ContinuousClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and groups all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"commands under a single global window. Within 300 ms of a previous","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"successfully executed command, the next one is cancelled. If the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"middleware is registered with ","type":"text"},{"code":"debugName: \"throttle\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the surfaced","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reason becomes ","type":"text"},{"code":".cancelled(.middleware(debugName: \"throttle\", command: …))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Per-command-keys","level":2,"text":"Per-command keys"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Group throttle windows by the command’s identity or shape:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment","code":["AnyNavigationMiddleware(","    ThrottleNavigationMiddleware<AppRoute>(interval: .milliseconds(300)) { command in","        if case .push(let route) = command {","            return \"push-\\(route)\"   \/\/ each push route gets its own window","        }","        return nil                    \/\/ other commands pass through","    }",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Return ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to opt a command out of throttling entirely.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Testing-with-an-injected-clock","level":2,"text":"Testing with an injected clock"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The middleware is generic over ","type":"text"},{"code":"Clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so tests can drive time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deterministically:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment","code":["let clock = TestClock()","let throttle = ThrottleNavigationMiddleware<AppRoute, TestClock>(","    interval: .milliseconds(300),","    clock: clock,","    key: { _ in \"all\" }",")","store.addMiddleware(AnyNavigationMiddleware(throttle), debugName: \"throttle\")","","store.send(.go(.home))","clock.advance(by: .milliseconds(50))","store.send(.go(.detail))         \/\/ cancelled — within window","","clock.advance(by: .milliseconds(400))","store.send(.go(.settings))       \/\/ accepted — beyond window"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Composing-with-whenCancelled","level":2,"text":"Composing with `.whenCancelled`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A throttle cancel surfaces as ","type":"text"},{"code":".cancelled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".whenCancelled(primary, fallback:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" treats a throttled command the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same as any other cancelled command:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment","code":["store.execute(","    .whenCancelled(","        .push(.detail),","        fallback: .push(.home)","    )",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the throttle middleware cancels the ","type":"text"},{"code":".push(.detail)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fallback ","type":"text"},{"code":".push(.home)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is attempted next. ","type":"text"},{"code":"NavigationStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"routes that fallback back through the full middleware chain, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"global throttle key can cancel the fallback too if it still lands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inside the same throttle window. Each leg runs behind an internal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"savepoint: if the fallback also fails or is cancelled, neither leg’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"partial state is committed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Debounce","level":2,"text":"Debounce?"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Debounce semantics — “wait N ms, then fire the latest” — live in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"DebouncingNavigator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not in ","type":"text"},{"code":"NavigationCommand","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". That keeps the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"engine synchronous while the async wrapper owns the timer,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cancellation, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" injection needed for deterministic tests.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Use throttle middleware for synchronous “reject too soon” behavior","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"DebouncingNavigator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for delayed “latest wins” behavior.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Next-steps","level":2,"text":"Next steps"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/NavigationStore-and-Hosts"},{"type":"text","text":" for the typed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onEvent"},{"type":"text","text":" callback and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStore.events"},{"type":"text","text":" stream that expose throttle cancellations."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/Tutorial-MiddlewareComposition"},{"type":"text","text":" for the broader"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"middleware composition story (logging, entitlement gating,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"analytics)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting"],["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting","doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/InnoRouterSwiftUI"]]},"references":{"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui/documentation/InnoRouterSwiftUI/NavigationStore-and-Hosts":{"abstract":[{"code":"RouterHost","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the default self-contained stack-plus-modal surface."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NavigationStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the advanced stack-only authority to use when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"application needs to own navigation state outside a host."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/NavigationStore-and-Hosts","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/innorouterswiftui\/navigationstore-and-hosts","title":"NavigationStore and hosts","type":"topic"},"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui/documentation/InnoRouterSwiftUI/Tutorial-MiddlewareComposition":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install logging, entitlement gating, and analytics middleware on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"both "},{"code":"NavigationStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"ModalStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Inspect the participant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discipline that pairs completion callbacks with the middlewares"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose "},{"code":"willExecute","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hook actually 